Z||000007||RedHaze86SD4||11-12-2001||03:27 PM||||My first Fiero was an 84 2m4 Sport Coupe. <A HREF="http://i3.yimg.com/3/eccc2d4a/g/a44e4b3a.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://i3.yimg.com/3/eccc2d4a/g/a44e4b3a.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://i3.yimg.com/3/eccc2d4a/g/fe2b8654.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://i3.yimg.com/3/eccc2d4a/g/fe2b8654.jpg</A> <BR>There were no SE tags anywhere. It was a 2.5 with auto. Power windows, man locks with black and dark grey interior.I got it Sept of 99 and it had 80k on it. On the stock speedo (85mph) I could wrap it around to the 5mph at 6000 rpm and was clocked (well running next to a firehawk with a digi dash) at over 140mph. Which was believable if you were in the car with me. It had great off the line power, but the top end was outrageous. Only mods I made to it were putting in Accel 8mm wires and performance dis. cap and coil. Also I busted out the restricter plate in the side intake panel and removed the restricter plate from under the TPI unit. Otherwise was stock as best as I could tell. Unfortunately it threw a belt at 75mph and it locked up the crank which toasted the block... Alas I should have kept it but needed new wheels..<P>------------------<BR>The Possabilities are only hindered by your imagination and will to make them come alive....<P>-=Red Haze.. Its coming=-<p>[This message has been edited by RedHaze86SD4 (edited 11-12-2001).]||||reg||1
